# ── Python ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/

# Virtual environments (never commit these)
venv/
.venv/
# Anchored to the repo root. An unanchored env/ matches at ANY depth, which
# silently swallowed sdi-intelligence-backend/env/ — configuration, not a
# virtualenv — and a file that cannot be committed is a file nobody can deploy.
/env/
.env
!config/*.example.env

# ── Output data (VERY IMPORTANT) ─────────────────────────────────────────
output/
*.json
# THE WEEKLY PARITY RESULT IS THE EXCEPTION, for the same reason the report PDFs are: it is
# written to be read on another machine, and week on week it is the record of whether the
# engine is converging on the estimators' own sheets. Scoped to reports/parity-*.json so a
# job's own output JSON is still refused everywhere. It holds no manual-estimate figure —
# tools/parity_workbooks.py writes variances, never the other side's pounds.
!reports/parity-*.json
*.jsonl
*.log
*.txt

# THE PRICE REGISTER IS THE OPPOSITE OF A RUN OUTPUT. It is SDI's commercial data, versioned
# on purpose so a rate change is reviewable in a diff without a code edit — which is the
# whole reason the figures were moved out of config.py. The blanket *.json above exists to
# keep job data and run outputs out of the repository; this is neither.
!data/price_register.json

# A confirmations file is an INPUT, not an output: what a person read off the drawing,
# entered once and ranked above everything the engine derived (src/estimator_confirmed.py).
# The *.json rule above exists to keep run outputs and job data out of the repo, and these
# are neither — they are small, hand-written, carry no customer geometry beyond overall
# sizes, and are worthless if they cannot be reviewed in a diff like any other statement
# of fact. Named narrowly so the blanket rule still holds everywhere else.
!tools/jobs/*.json
# A JOB'S RULINGS NOW LIVE IN config.JOB_DECISIONS, NOT IN A FILE HERE. "config needs to
# be in config files. not json files lying around and being copied manually around" —
# James Gray, 17 Sep 2026. A decision arrives with a pull, diffs like any other statement
# of fact, and cannot differ between two machines. The exception below stays only so that a
# stray answers file somebody drops in `docs/answers/` is VISIBLE in review rather than
# silently ignored; the engine still reads one written beside the drawings on the share.
!docs/answers/*.json

# ── Input data (drawings, spreadsheets) ──────────────────────────────────
input/

# PDFs, images and workbooks (CRITICAL — job data, never commit)
*.pdf
# THE STATUS REPORTS ARE THE EXCEPTION, and a narrow one.
#
# The rule above exists because a PDF in this repo is almost always job data — a customer's
# drawing pack — and that must never be committed. The status reports are the opposite kind
# of file: they are written to be read by other people, on other machines. The portal opens
# them from a share, and the machine that prints them is not the machine that serves them, so
# an ignored PDF is a report that exists for exactly one person.
#
# Scoped to reports/ and to PDF alone, so a drawing dropped anywhere else is still refused.
# tools/report_pdf.py prints them; test_a_status_report_ships_in_both_formats.py fails when
# one is missing or untracked.
!reports/*.pdf
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.xls
*.xlsx

# CAD exports are job data exactly as PDFs are — a DXF carries the customer's geometry.
# The fixtures under tests/ are already TRACKED, and a tracked file is unaffected by an
# ignore, so this costs the replay harness nothing.
*.dxf
*.DXF
*.dwg
*.DWG

# Generated deliverables. Named narrowly, NOT as a blanket *.html: docs/, reports/ and
# sdi-intelligence-backend/ are full of hand-written HTML that must stay committable, and
# the lesson at the foot of this file is that a broad ignore is a trap for the next file.
# These four patterns are what the engine itself writes beside a job:
#   job_report_html.py -> {stem}_report.html      client_quote_html.py -> {safe}_quote.html
#   also *_quote_LLM-ONLY.html and *.estimate_report.html
*_report.html
*.estimate_report.html
*_quote.html
*_quote_LLM-ONLY.html

# ── Backups / scratch ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.bak
*.bak_*
*.backup
*~

# SQL dumps (schema lives in versioned .sql under sql/ if needed)
*.sql

# ── OS ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ── Explicit keeps (override the broad ignores above) ────────────────────
# A BROAD IGNORE PLUS ONE EXCEPTION IS A TRAP FOR THE NEXT FILE. `*.txt` above
# means every new .txt is invisible to `git add -A`, which reports nothing —
# requirements-dev.txt was written, committed, pushed and merged before anybody
# noticed it had never left the machine it was created on. Anything meant to be
# kept has to be named here.
!requirements.txt
!requirements-dev.txt
# CLIENT QUOTATION DATA IS NOT SOURCE CODE.
# This line used to read "!corpus/*.jsonl" -- an explicit exception that put the client
# corpora BACK after the *.jsonl rule above had excluded them. With src/corpus.jsonl that
# was 104,386 quotation records in the repository: customer names, job numbers, sell
# prices, cost breakdowns, rebate fractions, derived overhead divisors, and the names of
# the 39 estimators who prepared them, spanning 2006-2036 and 488 customers.
#
# Nothing reads them at estimate time. They are an INTERMEDIATE ARTEFACT: corpus_ingest.py
# writes one from the K: spreadsheets, and ingest_historical_to_db.py / _to_qdrant.py read
# it once to load SQL Server and the vector store. Both take the path as an argument and
# default to a RELATIVE corpus.jsonl, not to anything committed here. The engine's
# corpus-derived numbers are constants in config.py, with the corpus named in a comment as
# their provenance -- the file itself is not consulted.
#
# So it bought nothing and put SDI's own margin structure, and its clients' pricing
# history, on an external code host. The exception is removed and the ignore above stands.
corpus/
cache/
.sdi-commit

# Frozen-replay harness: accepted facts and frozen summaries are versioned evidence
!tests/replay/**/*.json
